 the real STARK-composition wrap circuit (the remaining      M0.5-impl work) changes only the key this contract is deployed      with \\u2014 the verification equation, calldata encoding      (abi-encoded uint256[8]: A.x A.y B.x1 B.x0 B.y1 B.y0 C.x C.y) and      gas profile measured here carry over unchanged.\",\"kind\":\"dev\",\"methods\":{\"constructor\":{\"params\":{\"vk\":\"Verifying key words: alpha(2) || beta(4) || gamma(4) ||        delta(4) || ic0(2) || ic1(2) || ic2(2), G2 points in EVM        precompile order (x_c1, x_c0, y_c1, y_c0).\"}},\"verifyWrapped(bytes,bytes32)\":{\"params\":{\"proof\":\"Wrapped proof bytes (format defined by the wrap stage).\",\"publicInputsDigest\":\"SHA3-256 binding of (message || signer pks)        as computed by ThresholdVerifier.\"}}},\"stateVariables\":{\"PAIRING_GAS\":{\"details\":\"Gas bounds forwarded to the precompiles: a malformed point makes      a precompile consume everything it is given, so unbounded      forwarding would let an invalid proof burn the caller's whole      gas stipend (griefing). Generous multiples of the EIP-1108      costs (pairing: 45k + 34k/pair = 181k for 4 pairs).\"}},\"title\":\"Groth16WrapVerifier - IWrapVerifier over BN254 pairing precompiles\",\"version\":1},\"userdoc\":{\"kind\":\"user\",\"methods\":{},\"notice\":\"On-chain half of the M0.5-impl wrap path: verifies a BN254         Groth16 proof whose two public inputs are the 128-bit halves of         ThresholdVerifier's publicInputsDigest, binding the wrapped         proof to the exact message and signer set.\",\"version\":1}},\"settings\":{\"compilationTarget\":{\"src/Groth16WrapVerifier.sol\":\"Groth16WrapVerifier\"},\"evmVersion\":\"paris\",\"libraries\":{},\"metadata\":{\"bytecodeHash\":\"ipfs\"},\"optimizer\":{\"enabled\":true,\"runs\":200},\"remappings\":[\":@openzeppelin/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/\",\":@qs/=src/\",\":erc4626-tests/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/lib/erc4626-tests/\",\":forge-std/=lib/forge-std/src/\",\":halmos-cheatco